31,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My research shows that while targeted trials like the call-back program can significantly reduce readmissions, they fail once support ends. Furthermore, joint clinics often collapse due to disputes over budgets and rotas.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The physical capacity is strained. Outpatient rooms and parking are full by mid-morning, and the shuttle coverage is insufficient for most of the district. Our booking system also fails to capture any activity without a fixed appointment.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems our external dependencies are rather fragile. Data agreements with outside surgeries are an administrative marathon, and shared nursing rounds are frequently thwarted by the simple reality of locked gates and bad weather.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I've found that our ward nursing posts have some big gaps, and we're relying on agency cover way too much! But on the bright side, the midwifery rota actually has some lovely slack.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is a sobering reality that our development allocation has shrunk by nearly a quarter, and we must now pay for floor space from this same pot. Furthermore, only on-site sessions generate regional fund tariffs. We must be mindful of this.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if we must pay for floor space from the development pot, we cannot afford a project that requires new physical infrastructure or complex joint-departmental management.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, I agree. Given that parking and rooms are already at capacity by mid-morning, any program that increases physical footfall without a streamlined booking process will likely cause the system to seize up.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, a fascinating point. If we invite more patients into a system that is already gasping for air, we aren't providing care; we are simply managing a queue in a parking lot.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, that sounds so stressful! We really need to be careful. If the ward nurses are already struggling with vacancies, adding more pressure to them would be heartbreaking. We should look for something that helps!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"It is a gentle reminder that we must not only build for today but ensure we can sustain the work tomorrow. If on-site sessions are our only source of revenue, we must prioritize stability over expansion.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, I agree that we must avoid adding pressure to the ward staff. We should prioritize a program that is sustainable and doesn't rely on the fragile joint-departmental structures I found in the board minutes.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, if on-site sessions are the only revenue source, but our rooms and parking are already full, we have a contradiction. We cannot increase revenue if we cannot physically fit more patients.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, a delightful paradox indeed. We are essentially being asked to fill a glass that is already overflowing. Perhaps the solution lies in a program that optimizes our existing space rather than demanding more of it.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that does sound like a tricky puzzle! Maybe we can find a program that uses the slack in the midwifery rota? It would be so wonderful to use the help we already have!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Yumi, your optimism is a light in this room. Utilizing existing strengths, like the midwifery slack, is a wise path. We must seek a harmony between our available hands and our limited space.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"We must be cautious. If we choose a program that looks good on paper but lacks a permanent budget or clear ownership, it will simply become another buried initiative that fails the moment the trial ends.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. We must avoid any proposal that creates a hidden workload. If the booking system cannot track the activity, the program will eventually collapse under its own invisible weight.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. We must avoid the allure of a ""grand launch"" that inevitably dissolves into a bureaucratic nightmare. If a program requires a dozen signed agreements from outside surgeries, it is not a plan; it is a wish.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I completely agree! We should pick something that makes everyone's day a little easier and doesn't make our hardworking staff feel overwhelmed. Let's find a project that's truly helpful and sustainable!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"Wisdom teaches us that the most enduring structures are those built upon a foundation of truth. Let us look for a path that respects our budget, our space, and our people.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
51,2,4,pass,Servas,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
